   "source": [
    "1. Getting of rid of frequencies not part of the targeted insturment. For Banju song it seems to be 294 to 784"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "2f12462d-5fe5-424a-84c6-435165421ad9",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "ffmpeg -i ustadnoorbakesh.wav -af \"lowpass=f=?\" filtered.wav\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "24cc4322-5f3f-4daf-9cb7-60c3ead703bc",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Highpass and Lowpasses are not absolute cutoffs. They are just audio adjusters. The better way is this scary looking command. \n",
    "ffmpeg -i input.wav -af \"afftfilt=real='if(between(b,80,2500),re,0)':imag='if(between(b,80,2500),im,0)'\" cleaned.wav\n",
    "\n",
    "Create a custom command and use:\n",
    "ernie-sound-filter 193 1175 ustadnoorbakesh.wav cleaned.wav"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "a24019ad-d318-457c-93d6-2e3921af4d24",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Filtering out things whose amplitude is soft but distruptive to the model:\n",
    "ffmpeg -i input.mp3 -af \"agate=threshold=0.02:ratio=10\" output.mp3"
   ]
  }
 ],
